pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% NOT a forgery: an honest `red` step whose witness touches the variable of a degree-`i64::MIN`
% row, so the checker really does substitute into it. It is ACCEPTED before and after.
%
% This is the guard against the lazy fix. Refusing rows whose degree is extreme, or clamping the
% substituted degree to the type's range instead of escalating to arbitrary precision, would
% pass every negative case in this fixture and break this one.
f 2;
red 1 x3 >= 1 : x2 -> 1 x3 -> 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
